.TH SDL_SCANF_VARARG_FUNC 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SCANF_VARARG_FUNC \- Macro that annotates a vararg function that operates like scanf.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_SCANF_VARARG_FUNC( fmtargnumber ) __attribute__ (( format( __scanf__, fmtargnumber, fmtargnumber+1 )))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If we were to annotate
.BR fscanf :

.IP
.EX
int fscanf(FILE *f, const char *fmt, ...) SDL_PRINTF_VARARG_FUNCV(2);
.EE
.PP

This notes that the second parameter should be a scanf-style format string, followed by
.BR \[char46]\[char46]\[char46] \[char46]
The compiler or other analysis tools can warn when this doesn\(aqt appear to be the case\[char46]
.PP
On compilers without this annotation mechanism, this is defined to nothing\[char46]
.PP
This can (and should) be used with
.BR SDL_SCANF_FORMAT_STRING
as well, which between them will cover at least Visual Studio, GCC, and Clang\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

